<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35668" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνῐ-αύσιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			4.180
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Hipp.</u>
			37
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			X.
			<u>Ages.</u>
			2.1
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			167
		</span></i> (Mylasa, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), etc.; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Th.
			4.117
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			5.1
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Mu.</u>
			400b21
		</span></i> (v.l.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνιαυτός</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a year, one year old,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.454
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				27.63
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίκτει ἡ θήλεια [ὗς] ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					545a29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>annual,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				15.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρτή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.180
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ τρίτῃ ἐπὶ τοῖς ἐνιαυσίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(5).593
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				5
			</span></i> (Ceos, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>): neut. pl. as Adv.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				449
			</span></i>. Regul.Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				462
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				1.113(4).11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>lasting a year,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				6.45
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. φυγή</span>
			<i>a year's</i> exile, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				37
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					775
				</span></i>
			 (dub.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεχειρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.117
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				5.15
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδός</span> X.l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἀνιαύσιος βεβώς</span> gone, absent <i>for
				a year,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				165
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
